 only gets 20% phase client  states that just like any sports team or  movie company or record company its  original deal with its gamers is based  on their talent and their perceived  value of that talent at the time of the  contract like any entertainment company  or sports team faze clan looks to  renegotiate a deal when the talent  starts to dramatically improve and this  is what the company alleges it is done  with t foo now this isn't terribly  relevant to t Fu's allegations that faze  clan actually breached the contract that  they in fact executed it's in fact sort  of an admission that their current  contract is unfair but since T foo isn't  really arguing unconscionability it  probably doesn't hurt them too much to  argue the optics of things and say that  they're offering a new contract in  recognition of T Foods Fortnight  abilities faze clan says it has offered  him a seven-figure bonus and some  options that give T V 100% of any deals  they negotiated for him according to  faze clan t foo has failed to respond to  any or all of these overtures as early  as September 28th of last year we sent  the first revised version of a contract  for T foo we sent him a new agreement to  his lawyer January 24th of this year we  sent another updated thought on April  3rd then again on April 29th we gave him  so many different options that had  little or even some of them had no money  going to faze clan and yet we still  couldn't get a deal done and we come to  find that the reason why is he never  plan on getting a deal done with us he  wanted to start a competing organization  now whether T foo has ignored faze clans  overtures or whether he wants to start a  competing company as faze clan alleges  probably won't have much effect on the  lawsuit itself the future conduct of the  parties doesn't really have much bearing  on the actual facts as they exist now  and in the past faze clan also disputes  the notion that the contracts are  predatory in its Twitter statement the  company notes that over the last several  months it has encouraged any faze clan  member interested in hiring an outside  manager or agent to do so but faze clans  best strategy may be to actually lean in  to the draconian terms of the current  contract phase client recognizes the  50/50 split and sometimes 2080 split in  the contract it argues that it has never  collected its 80 percent now assuming  that faze clan actually upheld its end  of the bargain faze clan could be  entitled to that 80 percent that's  actually written into the contract now  that the parties have broken up and are  going their separate ways  faze clan could go after it's 80 percent  as written in the contract from t fou  after all what does it have to lose  countersuing for 80 percent would give  faze clan a bargaining chip against t  foo additionally since faze clan and t  foo were unlikely to ever get back  together faze clan will probably want to  counterclaim for any projected amounts  that t food would have made during the  remaining period of the contract because  we were having these issues and because  we wanted Turner to feel that we had his  back we made the decision to not collect  any money under the under the old  agreement nothing from prize pool  nothing from YouTube nothing from  anything except for a couple of brand  deals that accepted that we only took  20% of and those deals came from us to  him if faze clan upheld its end of the  bargain in the contract then it would be  T Fuu who is the one who was breaching  the agreement by failing to play for  phase which would make him liable for  phases expectation damages during the  remaining years of the contract of  course that is a big if in either case  faze clan will want to show that it did  not breach the contract while T foo will  argue that they did breach the contract  I can't opine on the likelihood of  either situation because I don't know  the underlying facts that's what the  lawsuit is for the crucial question in  this litigation is whether faze clan  upheld its end of the bargain and gave T  Fuu everything he was entitled to under  the contract the crucial question is not  whether the contract is unfair to T Fuu  now T Fuu also filed a petition with the  California Labor Commissioner here T foo  makes some bold allegations about phase  clans activities T Fuu says that he was  pressured to drink before he turned 21  and faze clan encouraged him and other  residue  to gamble while on phase clamp property  teef who says that faze clan pressured  and expected residents of the phase  house to perform dangerous stunts which  resulted in t foods permanent injury the  labor commission petition argues that  gamers are entertainers and artists who  must be represented by licensed talent  agencies under California's talent  agency Act which regulates the  relationship between talent agencies and  their clients for tea food to be covered  by the talent agency Act among other  things he has to prove that he falls on  the definition of an artist under that  statute to me the labor commission  petition seems like the tail wagging the  dog in this litigation though certainly  not an expert in this particular niche  of California labor employment law so  feel free to view my analysis with  skepticism here but I do know my way  around California litigation and when  you go to the trouble of filing a  lawsuit you tend to throw everything  that you have at it  some arguments are better than others  and to me it feels like the labor  commission argument is colorable but  it's really just there to back up the  main breach of contract claim it's  possible that this petition could have  wide-ranging effects on the professional  gamer community if the talent agency Act  is expanding to cover them but this  seems like a claim that is probably  going to settle before getting to that  stage and setting new law but we'll see  how it unfolds  now instead of watching video games have  you ever thou